      {
        "id": 85443,
        "name": "Nielzabub",
        "username": "Nielzabub",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/{size}/1986_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-28T00:22:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think Moffat has done a great job at keeping with the continuity. My point was that his silliness isn't really any less than Davies's silliness. It's different, but not any worse. The reason Doctor Who has been able to survive for 50 years is because of its changing staff and dynamic nature. It can evolve and be relevant to any era. Silliness is just fine if it works in the context of the story being told, and most of the time it does. I do not think the show's integrity has ever really been compromised. It has always been a silly soft sci-fi show about a man with a magic box who travles through time and space trying to make things better for everyone that he can. Despite it's many changes, the show has managed to stay true to that course and remain popular and interesting.</p>",
