      {
        "id": 85447,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-07T22:15:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My thoughts aren't anything new. &nbsp;Like many, I thought Tennant's goodbye was a little too drawn out and lengthy, so I thought Matt Smith's was a nice contrast. &nbsp;I'm a little surprised that when he sent away Clara for the second time (right after swearing to her that he wouldn't) they didn't bring up the whole \"Rule #1: The doctor lies.\" thing, but whatever. &nbsp;Overall I liked the episode, and I thought it was an interesting explanation of the whole Trendzalore (sp?) thing.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As for silliness in Doctor Who, the near breaking point for me came with the whole galactic prison thing. &nbsp;&lt;SPOILER&gt; They spent several episodes building this whole thing about this unbreakable prison, and what/who could possibly be inside. &nbsp;Once he's imprisoned, how does he get out? &nbsp;He basically pulls a Bill and Ted, and after he gets out, he goes back and lets himself out (via Amy Pond). &nbsp;Wait what? &lt;/SPOILER&gt; &nbsp;&lt;- Is there a way to do that on here?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It bothered me a lot at first, and then I just kind of got over it, but now I reference it as an example any time someone tries to get overly \"technical\" about Doctor Who.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:07.802Z",
