      {
        "id": 85448,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-07T23:26:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Having finally watched it after being horribly ill and then on vacation, I will weigh in.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This is the most epic send-off any doctor has received. &nbsp;Far cry from the sad lay down and swap faces that the old ones got. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As to the story, I'm a fan of the old shows so all of the new stuff seems fast paced and full of glossing over things to move the story along too fast. &nbsp;I thought the plot fit his character, this doctor never let himself live in the past, always his mind on where he was, the Doctor who wouldn't look back. &nbsp;The regeneration energy as the most powerful weapon in existence was ridiculous, but excusable if you try hard enough, and the start of Capaldi went very well. &nbsp;Every Doctor gets bombed for his regeneration openning, and everyone gets over it and moves on.</p><p>I hope Capaldi brings in a slower style that actually develops characters and has the doctor find answers by doing more than pointing a screwdriver at everything. &nbsp;There are recurring characters that I don't feel like I have any idea who they are, and have a hard time caring about, in the old days you got a real good sense and attachment to characters that were only around for a story arc, or less in some cases.</p><p>Basically it was better than expected, but they still don't make them like they used to.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:07.876Z",
