      {
        "id": 85451,
        "name": "Nielzabub",
        "username": "Nielzabub",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/{size}/1986_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-08T01:29:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think most of the characters and plot were given as much time to develop as they needed to.They're not exactly in depth characters, but they're interesting and entertaining. The fast paced nature of the narrative also perfectly complemented Matt Smith's portrayel of the Doctor. the only characters in the Davies era other than the Doctor that I felt particularly attached to were Donna and Captain Jack. I've pretty much loved every side character introduced in the most recent era. Craig and the Pasternoster Gang are very fun and vibrant characters, and although there were times Amy needed to be slapped, I still found her story arc much more engaging and emotional than the Tween puppy love Rose had with the Doctor. I think Clara is a bit underrated as a companion. She's the only traveller in the new Who that hasn't just entirely abandoned her life to travel with the Doctor. She's kept a very clear line between her real life and her adventures. The romance angle was slightly forced and unnecessary, but I think&nbsp;it will be interesting to see how that changes now that the Doctor is an old man.</p><p>That being said, I do think this is a good time for a stylistic change, and I can definitely understand the want and need for a slower pacing. You can go only go so big before you need to start going small again.</p>",
